E AX3060 1033-recover-escape.ax:21:10-17 region-escape "a value allocated in the recovery point (reclaimed on abort) is stored into parameter `v` of `vecPush`, which lives in this function's own region (its caller's current region) - `vecPush` stores a value it allocates into that parameter" ^18:4-19:"this scope reclaims the stored value before the destination is used" ?"this store or call crosses a reclamation boundary: move it to the destination's outer scope, or keep the destination and every use inside the value's region; keeping another reference cannot postpone the reset"
E AX3090 1033-recover-escape.ax:30:6-21 recover-thunk-unseen "a recovery point's thunk has to be a lambda written at the call, or a top-level function" ?"an abort reclaims everything the thunk allocated, so the thunk is held to storing none of it anywhere older; that is checked on a lambda written here, and a top-level function captures nothing. Write the lambda at the call"
